        /// <para>Closing a file that has been written to does not guarantee the data has made it to physical media; it may remain in the operating system's file cache, for later writing to disk. This means that a successfully-closed file can be lost if the system crashes or loses power in this small window. To prevent this, call this function with the <c>flush</c> parameter set to true. This will make the operation take longer, and perhaps increase system load in general, but a successful result guarantees that the data has made it to physical storage. Don't use this for temporary files, caches, and unimportant data, and definitely use it for crucial irreplaceable files, like game saves.</para>
